==Battleground==
*5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>, delay 2~4 seconds<sup>60f~120f</sup>.
*1 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecat]] spawns after 4.67 seconds<sup>140f</sup>.
*5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 22 seconds<sup>660f</sup>, delay 2~4.67 seconds<sup>60f~140f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**20 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn, delay 2~8 seconds<sup>60f~240f</sup>.
**20 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn, delay 4~12 seconds<sup>120f~360f</sup>.
**20 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
**20 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecats]] spawn, delay 6~18 seconds<sup>180f~540f</sup>.
**1 [[Skelecat (Enemy)|Skelecat]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This is arguably one of the easiest [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]] due to the underwhelming health of each Skelecat (only 25,000 HP). Large groups of them can be easily demolished with Area Attack units or a large stack of [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cats]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cats]]. The aforementioned units' [[True Form]]s will help out tremendously if you have them.

